problem:
Problem description
- A single service location requires staffing over a planning horizon $$H$$ divided into $$T$$ equal time periods indexed by $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$.
- There is a set of allowed shift start times indexed by $$s \in \mathcal{S}$$. Each shift has a fixed duration $$L$$ and may continue across the end of the planning horizon if needed.
- Demand data $$d_t$$ gives the required number of salespeople in each period $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$.
- Coverage data $$a_{t,s}$$ indicates whether a salesperson starting shift $$s$$ is available in period $$t$$.
- Decision variables $$x_s$$ represent the number of salespeople assigned to each allowed shift start time $$s \in \mathcal{S}$$.
- The planning goal is to minimize the total number of salespeople scheduled while meeting all staffing requirements in every period.
- Business constraints:
  - Every time period must be staffed with at least the required number of salespeople.
  - Salespeople may only start work at the allowed shift start times.
  - Each salesperson works continuously for the full shift duration $$L$$ once assigned.
  - All staffing quantities must be nonnegative integers.
- A solution is represented by:
  - The integer assignment vector $$x = (x_s)_{s \in \mathcal{S}}$$.
  - The minimum total workforce size $$Z$$.

Input Format
{
  "H": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "planning horizon length"
  },
  "T": {
    "type": "integer",
    "meaning": "number of equal planning periods"
  },
  "period_length": {
    "type": "scalar $$\\Delta$$",
    "meaning": "length of each planning period"
  },
  "S": {
    "type": "integer",
    "meaning": "number of allowed shift start times"
  },
  "shift_duration": {
    "type": "scalar $$L$$",
    "meaning": "duration of each shift"
  },
  "shift_starts": {
    "type": "array of length $$S$$",
    "meaning": "allowed shift start times for each $$s \\in \\mathcal{S}$$"
  },
  "demand": {
    "type": "array of length $$T$$",
    "meaning": "required staffing level $$d_t$$ for each period $$t \\in \\mathcal{T}$$"
  },
  "coverage": {
    "type": "optional binary matrix of shape $$T \\times S$$",
    "meaning": "coverage indicator $$a_{t,s}$$, where $$1$$ means shift $$s$$ covers period $$t$$ and $$0$$ otherwise"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "total_salespeople": {
    "type": "integer",
    "meaning": "minimum total number of scheduled salespeople, denoted by $$Z$$"
  },
  "shift_assignments": {
    "type": "array of length $$S$$",
    "meaning": "integer values $$x_s$$ for each allowed shift start time $$s \\in \\mathcal{S}$$"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "H": 24,
  "T": 6,
  "period_length": 4,
  "S": 6,
  "shift_duration": 8,
  "shift_starts": ["02:00", "06:00", "10:00", "14:00", "18:00", "22:00"],
  "periods": [
    {"start": "02:00", "end": "06:00"},
    {"start": "06:00", "end": "10:00"},
    {"start": "10:00", "end": "14:00"},
    {"start": "14:00", "end": "18:00"},
    {"start": "18:00", "end": "22:00"},
    {"start": "22:00", "end": "02:00"}
  ],
  "demand": [10, 15, 25, 20, 18, 12]
}
